[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its reports hold more than
one problem. Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October:

- `parser`: **fixed** (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`). Ticket: [#1](https://github.com/lipinski/support-kb/issues/1).
- `hint`: **won't fix**. The booking-v3 form is retired. Ticket: [#2](https://github.com/lipinski/support-kb/issues/2).
- `one-day`: no fix named. The parser fix does not touch it. Ticket: [#3](https://github.com/lipinski/support-kb/issues/3).

<Callout kind="warn">
Each problem has its own ticket. Counts below are the desk's own view, built from the ticket export
at render time. One-day moves stay counted under their cause, as the desk files them.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

1. **`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant in #4471 writes the day
   first, so any day of 12 or less comes out with day and month swapped.
2. **`hint`: the booking-v3 form hint says `MM/DD/YYYY`.** The booking-v3 tenants write the day
   first and the form reads input their way, but the hint tells people to type the month first.
   Only reports through the form on booking-v3 tenants. Won't fix: the form is retired.
3. **`one-day`: dates move by one day.** Not a swap: the same meeting shows Tuesday in Lisbon and
   Monday in Toronto, and an invite can arrive dated before its booking. The desk noted these
   (`desk-notes.json`), but the kb filed them under `parser` by tenant. One reporter says they
   have stopped sending these, so the count is a floor.

## Why they were merged

- Triage merges by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). All these
  problems arrive under the same handful of subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Dates mixed
  up"), so they landed in one ticket.
- Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser locale. The cause depends on the tenant's locale
  and form, so the tags disagree with the cause in both directions (see the table).

## What to do

- Track each problem in its own ticket, linked above. A fix for one does not close the others.
- A new one-day report after 5 October is not the parser: reopen the `one-day` ticket.
- Read the body before you merge a date report: a swap and a one-day move look alike by subject.

